cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research, code, or datasets, please cite it as below."
title: "Latitude and Doubt: An exact ledger of meaning in messages"
abstract: "Shannon set the meaning of messages aside as irrelevant to the engineering problem. This paper restores it as bookkeeping. For a source that pairs what is meant, W, with what is said, X, the joint entropy divides exactly into three non-negative parts: the information the form conveys, I(W;X); the latitude Lat = H(X|W), which the speaker remains free to choose once the meaning is fixed; and the doubt Dbt = H(W|X), which the listener cannot recover from the form."
